rtant is explicit inclusion. Everyone is welcome means nothing without deliberate action. You have to make them welcomed in your community and you have them to feel it's real. And most of all, the power of menship. This is something that probably was the thing I cared about the most. uh you when you have the mentorship um in value in place you have people receiving but also people giving so you have someone believed in you before you did and this is receiving and at the same time these people are willing to give away what they know to new people and probably the last one is active maintenance. So community health require active maintenance, not passive hope, meaning that it's a lot of work. And this is probably why, you know, community work, quote, unquote, has become actually a job title, because it is a job, keeping up with the community, if you believe in the value of the community, of course. And all of this, to me, is Python community and this is what stay for the people means actually to me so at this point i like to look forward and but before that uh take what uh think about one person in this community who made a difference for you that is the value of the community so to wrap up looking forward and have questions to you, not conclusions, which I hope we can talk about later, is how do we engage with the generation that communicates differently? And how do we preserve depth in an age of fragmented attention? And finally, what can newcomers teach us about building communities? How can we learn from them and over to you what to stay for the people could mean to you thanks very much

